Z||000007||mrfiero||12-29-2000||10:37 PM||||Come on guys.....lighten up.  This is definitely a tongue-in-cheek site.  I know Jim Lund and he wouldn't bash the Fiero.....he owns several of them.  The cars pictures were already damaged (like the one with the roof caved in) and were purchased just for the parts that were left.<P>If you go to the main site ( <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.net</A>  ) you will see the link to "Salvagey Motors".   It says go here for a laugh.<P><BR>That said......if you look at the picture of vice president "T" you will see the front end of an '85 GT with lace wheels.  I used to own that car......it had a turbo quad 4 and Ryanes Slalom coilover suspension w/12" brakes.  Jeremy at the Fiero Factory now owns it......I miss that car!||||reg||10
Z||000008||theogre||12-29-2000||10:39 PM||||When I first started around the net looking for Fiero stuff that was one of the first I found. Having been in the towing/service business I thought it was funny as hell. It's a Dilbert or 5th Wave for the auto world. I'd lost the link to it. 10Q.||||reg||1
Z||000009||summerjim||12-30-2000||02:06 PM||||It's funny to see 2M4 Dale / Sean Heberly's post here about the amount of "spare" room in my skull.  He not only posted his comments here, but even sent me them in an email -- thanks!  (That's tongue-in-cheek... just like Salvagey Motors, in case you didn't catch it, Sean)<P>The page doesn't bash the Fiero... it satirizes conversions.<P>Don't worry -- we didn't smash any Fieros for Salvagey Motors.  Unless you count the one we dropped a tree on... maybe that video will surface someday.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
